    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The central idea of model quantization is representing the weights or activations of a model in a lower-precision format (such as 8-bit integers) rather than their original high-precision floatingpoint format</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Q( f i ) is the feature of quantized model.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">representing the weights or activations of a model in a lower-precision format (such as 8-bit integers) rather than their original high-precision floatingpoint format</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">calibrate (Nagel et al., 2020) quantized models</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ensuring that the quantized model retains much of its accuracy and functionality through training.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">INT2, INT3, and INT4 bit quantized variants of the 7 B and 13 B models</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a pre-quantized deep learning model description in standard ONNX format.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">representing the weights or activations of a model in a lower-precision format (such as 8-bit integers)</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">fine-tune the quantized model by minimizing L2</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Quantization [Morgan et al., 1991, Choi et al., 2018, Courbariaux et al., 2015, Zhang et al., 2018, Rastegari et al., 2016] transforms the representation of a models parameters from oating-point numbers (32-bit) into lower bit-widths</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-bit homogeneously quantized EfficientNet-Lite0</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">examine the effect of multi-threading on the latency of quantized models.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the output of the quantized model gradually deviates from the quantization-friendly zero-mean distribution.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">from FP16 to INT8 inevitably results in a decrease in model quality.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
