    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2401.18079_rag::chunk_000</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">For auto-regressive LLMs, caching key and value activations (KV cache) into memory is necessary for subsequent token generation.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">linear expansion of the Key-Value (KV) cache with the context length.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the generative inference of these LLMs typically incorporates the KV cache mechanism to improve the efficiency of computation resour</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KV cache activations surface as the dominant contributor to memory consumption during in</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
